THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

The header image (docs/figures/header/hippocampus-light.png and
hippocampus-dark.png) is cropped, cleaned and recoloured from:
  Title:   Drawing of the neural circuitry of the rodent hippocampus
  Author:  Santiago Ramon y Cajal (1852-1934)
  Year:    1911, Histologie du Systeme Nerveux de l'Homme et des Vertebres,
           A. Maloine, Paris
  Source:  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CajalHippocampus.jpeg
  Licence: public domain. The Commons page states: "This work is in the public
           domain in its country of origin and other countries and areas where
           the copyright term is the author's life plus 70 years or fewer." It
           was published in 1911, before 1929, so it is also in the public
           domain in the United States.

No other third-party material is redistributed in this repository. The optional
encoder step downloads, at install time and into the user's local store, the
Python packages onnxruntime, tokenizers and numpy from PyPI, and the
bge-small-en-v1.5 ONNX model files (Qdrant/bge-small-en-v1.5-onnx-Q on Hugging
Face, a quantized port of BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5, MIT licence as published on
its model card), each under its own licence. The model files are checked
against pinned sha256 digests. None of them is covered by the Apache License
of this repository.
